7592186385890 #edb/ref 1080 "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186385890 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385890 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8d10f141-9b73-597a-9894-f347066824f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385891 #edb/ref 1080 "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186385891 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385891 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3455f0ca-75c2-537a-9f24-93cc9bc1292f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385892 #edb/ref 1080 "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186385892 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385892 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6377c93b-2085-5845-a870-b47edaf10db1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388806 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388806 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140955" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388806 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388806 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}5\\sqrt{5} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ what is the second column of $U?$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186388806 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ded87b8e-27db-5dc9-a993-ea7145915541" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388806 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that if $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ and ${\\sigma }_{i}\\ne 0,$ then the $i$th column of $U$ can be found as\n\n$$\n{u}_{i}=\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{i}}A{v}_{i},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${u}_{i}$ and ${v}_{i}$ are the $i$th columns of the orthogonal matrices $U$ and $V,$ respectively.  \n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that the singular values are ${\\sigma }_{1}=5\\sqrt{5}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the first column of $U$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, we can't use the same formula to find the second column of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find a vector\n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nsuch that \n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,‖{u}_{2}‖=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nSolving ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{1}+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{2}=0,\n$$\n\nwe get a nonzero solution $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Normalizing this vector, we finally obtain the  second column of $U:$\n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186388807 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388807 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388807 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388807 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388807 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388812 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388807 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388807 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388807 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186388809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388807 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "081c1bc8-0f12-5c26-a32f-4ede9647ceec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388808 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186388808 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388808 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4e044b3e-0de0-5ba3-a1a8-c9c2af697d30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388809 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186388809 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388809 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9b1f2140-da8a-5a9a-ac9f-b7bd2a0eb0ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388810 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186388810 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388810 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3ae4669c-17b3-5dbd-b72e-85de2f92da19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388811 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186388811 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388811 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b74a318b-f896-579d-a51c-c6a72c3ae206" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388812 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186388812 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388812 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e41f43ff-e62a-520e-80f3-03f0e2518535" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404850 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404850 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95981" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404850 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404850 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{10} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186404850 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c0349f24-f5b9-5625-bd79-9fb74dd2ec96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404850 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: Notice that from the matrix $Σ,$ we can deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=\\sqrt{10}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$ without solving the characteristic equation.\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=10,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-10I & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}-10\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-10I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-0I & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}-0\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-0I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of $A{A}^{T}$): Since the first singular value is not zero, and we know the corresponding singular right vector, we can compute the first column of $U$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, we can't use the same formula to find the second column of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find a vector\n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nsuch that \n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,‖{u}_{2}‖=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nSolving ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{x}_{1}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{x}_{2}=0,\n$$\n\nwe get a nonzero solution $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Normalizing this vector, we finally obtain the  second column of $U:$ \n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186404851 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404851 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404851 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404851 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404851 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404851 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404851 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404851 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186404855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404851 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c3303f09-b1cf-58c2-80d3-c7c5d852de3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404852 #edb/ref 1080 "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186404852 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404852 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d5f1cb32-9a61-59b0-b216-f66534ffd075" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404853 #edb/ref 1080 "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186404853 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404853 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0bc0298a-ae5a-5828-9130-e084e0abf53d" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
